{:adr-id "2607152100"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-0141 (raising of cattle and buffaloes) ranch-operations-coordination actor"
 :status :accepted
 :date "2026-07-14"
 :deciders ["Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)"]
 :related ["ADR-2607122200" "ADR-2607011000"]

 :context
 "A prior attempt today scaffolded cloud-itonami-isic-0141 (docs/, test/, README.md)
  but pushed no src/ and no deps.edn while falsely claiming completeness/testedness.
  Caught in audit and reverted. This ADR codifies the corrected implementation,
  built from cloud-itonami-isic-1010 (meat processing) as the module-structure
  template, with clojure -M:test independently re-run before and after every push."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["direct animal handling (rancher's exclusive authority)"
  "veterinary treatment decisions (veterinarian/rancher authority)"
  "slaughter or culling decisions (economic and ethical authority remains human)"]

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-0141 with Governor, Facts, Registry, Store, Advisor,
  Phase, Operation, Sim (mirrors cloud-itonami-isic-1010 module-for-module):
  - Governor (RanchingOperationsGovernor): 5 hard checks (facility-not-registered,
    no-execution, treatment-or-slaughter-blocked, op-not-allowed, herd-count-invalid)
    + 3 escalation gates (always-escalate health concern, cost-threshold supply
    orders, low confidence < 0.7)
  - Facts: supply categories with cost thresholds (feed/veterinary-supply/equipment),
    species (cattle/buffalo)
  - Registry: independent pure predicates (cost-exceeds-threshold?,
    herd-count-non-positive?, confidence-below-floor?)
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore (registered-facility lookup)
  - Advisor: Advisor protocol + MockAdvisor (4 ops)
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout gate
  - Operation: composes advisor -> governor -> phase-gate (langgraph-clj wiring
    deferred, matching 1010's own stub)
  - Sim: demo runner with a working -main (1010's own -M:run is latent-broken --
    missing clojure.set require -- not inherited here)
  - Operations: log-herd-record, schedule-veterinary-visit,
    flag-animal-health-concern, order-supplies (closed allowlist, :effect :propose)
  - Tests: 30 tests / 90 assertions (facts, governor, phase, registry, store), all green
  - All .cljc (portable, no JVM interop), AGPL-3.0-or-later
  - README/operator-guide corrected to describe the real API (removed references
    to a nonexistent cattleops.actor/build-graph/approve! surface from the
    reverted prior attempt's docs)"

 :consequences
 {:positive
  ["Cattle-raising (0141) now genuinely implemented and fully tested, closing the
    gap left by the reverted prior attempt"
   "Scope boundaries (animal handling, treatment, slaughter/culling) hardcoded in
    governor checks, not just asserted in prose"
   "Animal-welfare escalation (flag-animal-health-concern always human) is a core
    design invariant"
   "Portable .cljc, zero JVM-only constructs, clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings"]
  :negative
  ["Real persistent store (Datomic/kotoba-server) is a follow-up (in-memory for now)"
   "langgraph-clj StateGraph wiring (real interrupt-before/checkpoint resume) is
    deferred scaffolding, matching 1010's own stub status"]}

 :verification
 {:test-count 30
  :assertion-count 90
  :test-status "0 failures, 0 errors -- independently re-verified from a fresh clone post-push"
  :lint-status "0 errors, 0 warnings"
